  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. All four new tests failed before the change and pass after it. The full test suite passes: 1910 passed, 102 skipped, 1 expected failure. Pytest also reported 31,000 tests as deselected; that comes from how the test run is configured, not from these tests, and I didn't look into it further.\n\n**The fix** (`src/click/core.py:392`): a subcommand now uses its own entry in the parent's `default_map` (`parent.default_map.get(info_name)`) instead of the parent's whole map. So `{\"sub\": {\"port\": 5000}}` gives `port=5000` to `sub`. A subcommand with no entry falls back to its own defaults.\n\n**Tests added** in `tests/test_defaults.py`:\n- A group's map sets a subcommand option, whether it comes from `context_settings` or `invoke(default_map=...)`. The option's source is reported as `DEFAULT_MAP`.\n- A sibling subcommand with no entry keeps its own default.\n- Nested groups (group, then group, then command) each read their own level of the map.\n- In a chained group, each subcommand gets its own entry.\n\n**Changelog:** 8.5.0 was already released, so I added a new \"Version 8.5.1 / Unreleased\" section at the top of `CHANGES.md`. There's no issue or PR number in the entry; add one if you have it.\n\nNothing is committed yet. Tell me if you want a commit or a PR.",
